course: dictionary
lesson: 7023
title: Learning a word from its context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You may meet a word you have never seen before. Do not stop at it. Read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «Parrotfish bite algae off coral with beak-like teeth» tells you a parrotfish is an animal that eats coral, and that its mouth is shaped like a beak.
explain: The sentence «one big parrotfish can make hundreds of kilos of sand a year» gives another clue. Sand does not usually come out of a fish, so the words point to a fish that grinds up coral and passes it out as sand. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then put your idea into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: A dictionary settles what the clues only suggest. A parrotfish is a brightly coloured fish of coral reefs, with teeth joined into a beak like a parrot's. The clues were right, and the dictionary gives the exact meaning.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A parrotfish is a brightly coloured fish of coral reefs.
fact: Its teeth are joined into a beak like a parrot's.
fact: It scrapes and bites coral to eat the algae on it.
fact: Parrotfish keep coral reefs healthy, and much of the white sand on tropical beaches can come from them.
exercise: What is a parrotfish? | A bird that lives high in trees | *A brightly coloured fish of coral reefs | A coral that grows in shallow sand | A parrot that can swim
exercise: «Walk on a white tropical beach and much of the sand under your feet may have passed through a parrotfish.» What does this sentence suggest about the sand? | It has never been in the sea | It was carried there by a storm | *Some of it may have come out of a parrotfish | It is made of broken shells only
exercise: Nadia says a parrotfish is a parrot that swims. What does the word really mean? | A bird that lives on coral | A fish that lives only in rivers | *A fish with a beak-like mouth, like a parrot's | A parrot that swims in the sea
test: What does a parrotfish do to coral? | It hides inside the coral all day | *It scrapes and bites coral to eat the algae on it | It builds coral into tall castles | It sings to other fish
test: Which words in «one big parrotfish can make hundreds of kilos of sand a year» are the strongest clue that parrotfish make sand? | *hundreds of kilos of sand | can make | one big parrotfish | a year
exam: «Some parrotfish sleep in a bubble of slime.» What does this sentence tell you? | They sleep on top of the coral in the sun | They never sleep at all | *They can rest inside a bubble of slime | They swim fast all night long
